 "notes": [
  "The parent's serial IRQ processes each transfer and HBlank starts the next one; link_packet is a coroutine advanced by link_service() each main-loop iteration.",
  "Waiting for peers, the bootstrap, keepalives and lobby packets yield to the game after 8 frames; in-game events are delivered without yielding so the presentation clock stays exact.",
  "Longest main-loop stall by the link during session start (instrumented build, roles scenario 1): 8 frames with 2 and 3 consoles, versus 42.8 (2 consoles) and 116.1 (3 consoles) frames before.",
  "Event latency is unchanged: in-game events still stop the host for their delivery."
 ],
 "limitations": [
  "mGBA only; no physical GBA, Pizza Boy Advance or frontend display buffering."
 ]
